proof_plan:
Define $\size x_p = p^{-\map {
u_p} x}$, where $\map {
u_p} x$ is the exponent of $p$ in $x$.
As $\map {
u_p} {x y} = \map {
u_p} x + \map {
u_p} y$, $\size \cdot_p$ is multiplicative.

As $\map {
u_p} {x + y} \ge \min \set {\map {
u_p} x, \map {
u_p} y}$, the [[Definition:Ultrametric Inequality|ultrametric inequality]] holds, which implies the [[Triangle Inequality]].

Metric consequences transfer, such as completeness and the [[Definition:Convergent Series|convergence]] of absolutely convergent series.
Order-theoretic ones fail: $\Q_p$ is not an [[Definition:Ordered Field|ordered field]], and a series converges {{iff}} its terms tend to $0$.
{{qed}}
